Why was WebSocket introduced?

Before WebSockets, web applications mainly used HTTP.

Problem with HTTP

HTTP follows a Request → Response model.

Browser sends a request.
Server sends a response.
Connection closes.

Example:

Client ---- Request ----> Server
Client <--- Response ---- Server
(Connection Closed)

If the server wants to send new data:

Client must send another request.
Server cannot send data on its own.

This causes:

More network traffic.
Increased latency.
Not suitable for real-time applications.
Example Problem

Imagine a chat application.

Without WebSockets:

User A sends message.
User B's browser keeps asking:

"Any new message?"
"Any new message?"
"Any new message?"

This is called Polling.

Problems:

Too many unnecessary requests.
Wastes bandwidth.
Slow updates.

WebSockets solve this problem.